11	// This TU is the missing seam: it is globbed INTO _ops (no own pybind module), is
12	// compiled with -DSG_TUNED_GEMM_IMPL=1 (the in-source #define below) so it links the
13	// wgmma branch of fused_mamba_megakernel.cuh, and exposes ONE non-template host
14	// launcher whose boundary is plain pointers/ints + the FusedScalars POD — NO
15	// header-only types (MambaTokenCtx / FusedOptState) cross the boundary — so
16	// dispatch.cpp can extern-declare it with only the mirror structs it already has. It
17	// calls ONLY launch_fused_mamba_megakernel_tc (the TC launcher); it never
18	// instantiates the scalar launcher template, so it CANNOT collide (ODR/duplicate-
19	// symbol) with the scalar mega_mamba_real_adamw.cu TU even though both are in _ops.
20	// The TC activations/grad workspace is sized DIFFERENTLY from the scalar
21	// MambaScratch partials (mb_tc_workspace_floats), so this TU owns its own cached
22	// scratch internally — dispatch.cpp passes no workspace for the TC path.
